{offset200}{ia10}{offset0}
{arialbld}Bob Renard{arial}
Military Advisor 
Royal Palace of Jaffa











My father-in-law, Ibn Yussef Wahim Al Khadin, the King of Jaffa, awaits you in his palace, he has decreed a national holiday of five days in honour of the Normo and Schyzo liberators.

The Jaffaris have adopted you as one of their own, they are arriving from everywhere to attend your triumph.
 
You should arrive from the Eastern Gate, where your troops entered the city, this avenue will henceforth be known as {arialbld}Avenue {name}{arial}, you will be escorted by 350 of my Azrakins, the blue warriors who do not know fear.

I advise you to abandon your jeep at the city limits for a more prestigious vessel in Jaffari eyes, your camel Sirokko of course, as this animal has become just as famous as you. This will cause a real sensation, the women are very sentimental about it.

Ten of my bravest Azrakins wish to be appointed to your personal guard.
They have made the pledge: Wherever you go, at your side they will stay; Wherever they may lurk, your enemies they will fight.

Finally, for having vainquished his enemies, the King has entrusted me to present to you on behalf of the Jaffari people, {arialbld}the Star of Tha'lab-Al-Sarawa{arial}, the highest distinction in the Order of the Desert Lords, the lion in his den trembles at his approach. 

This medal represents the three Touareg virtues, implacable like the sun, wise like the desert and generous like the camel...


{offset100}In the Name of his Serenity Ibn Yussef Wahim Al Khadin

His Military Advisor


{offset150}{arialbld}Bob Renard{arial}



